import os
FILES = {'README.md': '# Machine Learning Internship Projects – UCT\n* [Project 4 – Prediction of Agriculture Crop Production in India](project4_crop_production/)\n* [Project 5 – Crop and Weed Detection](project5_crop_weed_detection/)\n\nEach folder contains the code and a project report (`README.md`: company, background, problem statement, design, implementation, results, learnings).\n', 'project5_crop_weed_detection/requirements.txt': 'ultralytics>=8.3\nopencv-python>=4.8\nnumpy>=1.24\nmatplotlib>=3.7\nPyYAML>=6.0\ntensorflow>=2.13   # only needed for src/augment.py (Keras ImageDataGenerator)\n', 'project5_crop_weed_detection/README.md': '# Project 5 – Crop and Weed Detection\n\n**Machine Learning Internship – UCT** · Area: Agriculture\n\n## 1. Company\nUCT – machine-learning internship programme covering agriculture, predictive maintenance, smart city and industrial manufacturing.\n\n## 2. Background\nWeeds compete with crops for nutrients, water and land, reducing yield. Farmers usually spray pesticide over the whole field, wasting chemicals and leaving residues on crops. The dataset contains **1300 images (512×512 RGB)** of sesame crop and weeds, labelled with bounding boxes in **YOLO format**.\n\n## 3. Problem statement and relevance\nDetect and localise *crop* vs *weed* in field images so that a sprayer can treat **only weeds**. This reduces pesticide use, cost and crop contamination.\n\n## 4. Design\n```\nphotos (4000×3000) → cleaning (589→546) → resize 512×512 → augmentation (→1300) → manual YOLO labels\n      → train/val/test split (70/20/10, grouped to avoid leakage) → YOLOv8 → detections → spray planner → nozzle commands\n```\n* **Detector:** YOLOv8 (nano by default, `--model yolov8s.pt` for more accuracy), transfer learning from COCO weights.\n* **Classes:** `0 = crop`, `1 = weed` (change `CLASS_NAMES` if your label files differ).\n* **Spray logic:** `spray_planner.py` discards low-confidence weeds and weeds overlapping a crop box, then opens the nozzle lane containing each remaining weed.\n\n## 5. Implementation\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `src/augment.py` | Resize originals to 512×512 and grow the set to ~1300 images with flips + brightness/contrast jitter; transforms labels consistently |\n| `src/prepare_dataset.py` | Splits into train/val/test (augmented copies of one photo stay in the same split) and writes `data.yaml` |\n| `src/train.py` | Trains YOLOv8, evaluates on the test split (mAP, precision, recall) |\n| `src/predict.py` | Inference on images/folders/video, saves annotated output, prints nozzle plan |\n| `src/spray_planner.py` | Detections → selective-spray commands (unit-testable, no model needed) |\n\nRun:\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n# dataset already has 1300 labelled images:\npython src/prepare_dataset.py --raw data/raw --out data/yolo\npython src/train.py --data data/yolo/data.yaml --epochs 100\npython src/predict.py --weights outputs/crop_weed/weights/best.pt --source data/yolo/images/test\n```\nDataset: Google Drive link in the internship brief (extract to `data/raw/images` and `data/raw/labels`).\n\n## 6. Results\n> Fill in after training (`outputs/crop_weed/results.png`, confusion matrix, PR curves are generated by Ultralytics).\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---|\n| mAP@0.5 | _ |\n| mAP@0.5:0.95 | _ |\n| Precision | _ |\n| Recall | _ |\n\nAdd 3–4 annotated prediction images from `outputs/predictions/`.\n\n## 7. Learnings\n* Data quality matters more than model size: removing bad photos (589→546) and consistent labelling drove results.\n* Augmented copies of the same photo must stay in one split, otherwise validation scores are inflated.\n* Normalised YOLO labels make resizing trivial; flips need the box centre mirrored (`x → 1-x`).\n* Limitations: one crop (sesame), one field/season; lighting and growth-stage changes may hurt generalisation. Augmented data is not a substitute for new field images.\n* Future work: more crops and conditions, segmentation for overlapping plants, deployment on Jetson/Raspberry Pi with real nozzle hardware.\n', 'project5_crop_weed_detection/src/prepare_dataset.py': '"""Split the 1300-image YOLO dataset into train/val/test and write data.yaml.\n\nExpected raw layout (images and YOLO .txt labels side by side or in two folders):\n    data/raw/images/*.jpg   data/raw/labels/*.txt\nUsage: python src/prepare_dataset.py --raw data/raw --out data/yolo\nClass ids (edit CLASS_NAMES if your labels differ): 0 = crop (sesame), 1 = weed\n"""\nimport argparse, random, shutil\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport yaml\n\nCLASS_NAMES = ["crop", "weed"]\nEXT = {".jpg", ".jpeg", ".png"}\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument("--raw", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument("--out", default="data/yolo")\n    ap.add_argument("--split", type=float, nargs=3, default=[0.7, 0.2, 0.1])\n    ap.add_argument("--seed", type=int, default=42)\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n    raw, out = Path(a.raw), Path(a.out)\n    img_dir = raw / "images" if (raw / "images").is_dir() else raw\n    lbl_dir = raw / "labels" if (raw / "labels").is_dir() else raw\n\n    imgs = sorted(p for p in img_dir.iterdir() if p.suffix.lower() in EXT)\n    pairs = [(i, lbl_dir / f"{i.stem}.txt") for i in imgs if (lbl_dir / f"{i.stem}.txt").exists()]\n    print(f"{len(imgs)} images, {len(pairs)} with labels")\n    if not pairs:\n        raise SystemExit("No image/label pairs found.")\n\n    # Augmented copies of one photo must not straddle splits; group by stem prefix\n    # before \'_aug\' if present, so leakage is avoided.\n    groups = {}\n    for i, l in pairs:\n        groups.setdefault(i.stem.split("_aug")[0], []).append((i, l))\n    keys = sorted(groups); random.Random(a.seed).shuffle(keys)\n    n = len(keys); c1 = int(a.split[0] * n); c2 = c1 + int(a.split[1] * n)\n    parts = {"train": keys[:c1], "val": keys[c1:c2], "test": keys[c2:]}\n\n    for split, ks in parts.items():\n        (out / "images" / split).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        (out / "labels" / split).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        for k in ks:\n            for i, l in groups[k]:\n                shutil.copy(i, out / "images" / split / i.name)\n                shutil.copy(l, out / "labels" / split / l.name)\n        print(split, sum(len(groups[k]) for k in ks), "images")\n\n    cfg = {"path": str(out.resolve()), "train": "images/train", "val": "images/val",\n           "test": "images/test", "names": {i: n for i, n in enumerate(CLASS_NAMES)}}\n    (out / "data.yaml").write_text(yaml.safe_dump(cfg, sort_keys=False))\n    print("Wrote", out / "data.yaml")\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n', 'project5_crop_weed_detection/src/spray_planner.py': '"""Turns detections into selective-spray commands.\n\nCore idea of the project: only spray where a *weed* is detected, and never where a\ncrop box overlaps the target. Pure Python/NumPy so it can be unit-tested without a model.\n"""\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\nWEED, CROP = 1, 0  # keep in sync with CLASS_NAMES in prepare_dataset.py\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Det:\n    cls: int\n    conf: float\n    box: Tuple[float, float, float, float]  # x1, y1, x2, y2 in pixels\n\n\ndef iou(a, b) -> float:\n    ix1, iy1, ix2, iy2 = max(a[0], b[0]), max(a[1], b[1]), min(a[2], b[2]), min(a[3], b[3])\n    inter = max(0, ix2 - ix1) * max(0, iy2 - iy1)\n    ua = (a[2] - a[0]) * (a[3] - a[1]) + (b[2] - b[0]) * (b[3] - b[1]) - inter\n    return inter / ua if ua else 0.0\n\n\ndef plan_spray(dets: List[Det], img_w=512, n_nozzles=8, min_conf=0.4, max_crop_overlap=0.2):\n    """Return (set of nozzle indices to open, list of weed boxes accepted)."""\n    crops = [d for d in dets if d.cls == CROP and d.conf >= min_conf]\n    targets = []\n    for d in dets:\n        if d.cls != WEED or d.conf < min_conf:\n            continue\n        if any(iou(d.box, c.box) > max_crop_overlap for c in crops):\n            continue  # too close to a crop -> skip to avoid pesticide on crop\n        targets.append(d)\n    # One nozzle lane per weed: the lane containing the weed\'s horizontal centre.\n    # Lanes are never opened for a weed that overlaps a crop (filtered above).\n    width = img_w / n_nozzles\n    nozzles = {min(int(((t.box[0] + t.box[2]) / 2) // width), n_nozzles - 1) for t in targets}\n    return sorted(nozzles), targets\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    demo = [Det(CROP, .9, (50, 100, 120, 200)), Det(WEED, .8, (300, 120, 360, 180)),\n            Det(WEED, .7, (60, 110, 110, 190))]\n    print(plan_spray(demo))\n', 'project5_crop_weed_detection/src/predict.py': '"""Run inference + spray planning on an image/folder/video.\nUsage: python src/predict.py --weights outputs/crop_weed/weights/best.pt --source data/yolo/images/test\n"""\nimport argparse\nfrom ultralytics import YOLO\nfrom spray_planner import Det, plan_spray\n\nap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\nap.add_argument("--weights", required=True); ap.add_argument("--source", required=True)\nap.add_argument("--conf", type=float, default=0.4)\na = ap.parse_args()\n\nmodel = YOLO(a.weights)\nfor r in model.predict(a.source, conf=a.conf, save=True, project="outputs", name="predictions", stream=True):\n    dets = [Det(int(c), float(p), tuple(map(float, b))) for c, p, b in\n            zip(r.boxes.cls, r.boxes.conf, r.boxes.xyxy)]\n    nozzles, targets = plan_spray(dets, img_w=r.orig_shape[1], min_conf=a.conf)\n    print(f"{r.path}: {len(targets)} weeds -> open nozzles {nozzles}")\n', 'project5_crop_weed_detection/src/augment.py': '"""Reproduces the data-augmentation step of the data preparation (546 -> ~1300 images).\nFlip augmentations (so YOLO boxes can be\ntransformed exactly) plus brightness/contrast jitter (equivalent in spirit to Keras ImageDataGenerator).\n\nUsage: python src/augment.py --images data/clean/images --labels data/clean/labels --out data/raw --target 1300\n"""\nimport argparse, random\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport cv2, numpy as np\n\n\ndef read_labels(p):\n    rows = [l.split() for l in p.read_text().strip().splitlines() if l.strip()]\n    return [(int(r[0]), *map(float, r[1:5])) for r in rows]\n\n\ndef write_labels(p, boxes):\n    p.write_text("\\n".join(f"{c} {x:.6f} {y:.6f} {w:.6f} {h:.6f}" for c, x, y, w, h in boxes))\n\n\ndef hflip(img, b):  return img[:, ::-1], [(c, 1 - x, y, w, h) for c, x, y, w, h in b]\ndef vflip(img, b):  return img[::-1], [(c, x, 1 - y, w, h) for c, x, y, w, h in b]\ndef both(img, b):   return hflip(*vflip(img, b))\n\n\ndef jitter(img, rng):\n    img = img.astype(np.float32)\n    img = img * rng.uniform(0.75, 1.25) + rng.uniform(-20, 20)       # contrast / brightness\n    return np.clip(img, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument("--images", required=True); ap.add_argument("--labels", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument("--out", required=True); ap.add_argument("--target", type=int, default=1300)\n    ap.add_argument("--size", type=int, default=512); ap.add_argument("--seed", type=int, default=42)\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n    rng, r = np.random.default_rng(a.seed), random.Random(a.seed)\n    out_i, out_l = Path(a.out, "images"), Path(a.out, "labels")\n    out_i.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True); out_l.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n    srcs = [p for p in sorted(Path(a.images).iterdir()) if p.suffix.lower() in {".jpg", ".jpeg", ".png"}\n            and Path(a.labels, p.stem + ".txt").exists()]\n    count = 0\n    for p in srcs:  # 1) resize originals 4000x3000 -> 512x512 (YOLO labels are normalised, so unchanged)\n        img = cv2.resize(cv2.imread(str(p)), (a.size, a.size), interpolation=cv2.INTER_AREA)\n        cv2.imwrite(str(out_i / f"{p.stem}.jpg"), img)\n        write_labels(out_l / f"{p.stem}.txt", read_labels(Path(a.labels, p.stem + ".txt")))\n        count += 1\n    ops = [hflip, vflip, both]\n    while count < a.target:  # 2) fill up to target with augmented copies\n        p = r.choice(srcs)\n        img = cv2.imread(str(out_i / f"{p.stem}.jpg")); b = read_labels(out_l / f"{p.stem}.txt")\n        img, b = r.choice(ops)(img, b)\n        img = jitter(np.ascontiguousarray(img), rng)\n        name = f"{p.stem}_aug{count}"\n        cv2.imwrite(str(out_i / f"{name}.jpg"), img); write_labels(out_l / f"{name}.txt", b)\n        count += 1\n    print(f"Wrote {count} images to {a.out}")\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n', 'project5_crop_weed_detection/src/train.py': '"""Train YOLOv8 on the crop/weed dataset.\nUsage: python src/train.py --data data/yolo/data.yaml --model yolov8n.pt --epochs 100\n"""\nimport argparse\nfrom ultralytics import YOLO\n\nap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\nap.add_argument("--data", required=True)\nap.add_argument("--model", default="yolov8n.pt")\nap.add_argument("--epochs", type=int, default=100)\nap.add_argument("--imgsz", type=int, default=512)\nap.add_argument("--batch", type=int, default=16)\nap.add_argument("--device", default=None)\na = ap.parse_args()\n\nmodel = YOLO(a.model)\nmodel.train(data=a.data, epochs=a.epochs, imgsz=a.imgsz, batch=a.batch, device=a.device,\n            project="outputs", name="crop_weed", patience=20, seed=42)\nm = model.val(data=a.data, split="test")\nprint(f"Test mAP50={m.box.map50:.3f}  mAP50-95={m.box.map:.3f}  P={m.box.mp:.3f}  R={m.box.mr:.3f}")\n', 'project4_crop_production/requirements.txt': 'pandas>=2.0\nnumpy>=1.24\nscikit-learn>=1.3\nmatplotlib>=3.7\njoblib>=1.3\n', 'project4_crop_production/README.md': "# Project 4 – Prediction of Agriculture Crop Production in India\n\n**Machine Learning Internship – UCT** · Area: Agriculture\n\n## 1. Company\nUCT – machine-learning internship programme covering agriculture, predictive maintenance, smart city and industrial manufacturing.\n\n## 2. Background\nIndia is the second most populous country (1.3 billion+) and agriculture is the main livelihood for a large share of its people. Production varies strongly with crop, season, location and cultivated area. The dataset (2001–2014, from data.gov.in, openly licensed) records crop cultivation and production across states.\n\n## 3. Problem statement and relevance\nPredict the **production** of a crop given crop, state/zone, season, year and cultivated area (and cost where available). Reliable estimates help farmers choose crops, help planners with procurement/storage, and flag shortfalls early.\n\n## 4. Design\n```\nraw CSV → cleaning → feature prep → ColumnTransformer → model → evaluation → saved pipeline\n                    (log1p target)  (impute+scale | one-hot)   (Ridge / RF / GBM)\n```\n* **Target:** `production`, modelled as `log1p(production)` because it is extremely right-skewed (sugarcane vs. sesame differ by orders of magnitude). Metrics are reported both in log space and in original units.\n* **Features:** numeric (area/quantity, year, cost) and categorical (state, district, season, crop, variety, recommended zone). Column names are auto-detected, so both the data.gov.in layout and the brief's layout work.\n* **Models compared:** Ridge (baseline), Random Forest, Gradient Boosting, tuned with 3-fold `GridSearchCV`; 80/20 train/test split, seed 42.\n\n## 5. Implementation\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `src/train.py` | Cleaning, preprocessing, training, tuning, metrics, plots, saves `outputs/best_model.joblib` |\n| `src/predict.py` | Predict production for new rows from a CSV |\n| `src/make_synthetic_data.py` | Synthetic data for smoke-testing only – **not** used for reported results |\n\nRun:\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\npython src/train.py --data data/crop_production.csv\npython src/predict.py --input new_rows.csv\n```\nPlace the dataset (Google Drive link in the internship brief) at `data/crop_production.csv`.\n\n## 6. Results\n> Fill in after running on the real dataset (`outputs/metrics.json`, plots in `outputs/`).\n\n| Model | R² (log) | R² | RMSE | MAE |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ridge | _ | _ | _ | _ |\n| Random Forest | _ | _ | _ | _ |\n| Gradient Boosting | _ | _ | _ | _ |\n\nPlots: `outputs/actual_vs_predicted.png`, `outputs/feature_importance.png`, `outputs/model_comparison.png`.\n\n## 7. Learnings\n* Log-transforming a heavy-tailed target is essential; raw-unit R² is dominated by a few very large crops.\n* Tree ensembles handle the mixed categorical/numeric data and interactions (crop × area) far better than a linear baseline.\n* Rows with missing production must be dropped, not imputed, to avoid training on fabricated targets.\n* Limitations: no weather/rainfall/soil data; a random split can leak the same district-year across train and test – a year-based split would be a stricter test.\n* Future work: add rainfall/temperature, try CatBoost/LightGBM, hold out whole years.\n", 'project4_crop_production/src/predict.py': '"""Predict production for new rows: python src/predict.py --model outputs/best_model.joblib --input new.csv"""\nimport argparse, re\nimport joblib, numpy as np, pandas as pd\n\nap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\nap.add_argument("--model", default="outputs/best_model.joblib")\nap.add_argument("--input", required=True)\na = ap.parse_args()\ndf = pd.read_csv(a.input)\ndf.columns = [re.sub(r"[^a-z0-9]+", "_", c.strip().lower()).strip("_") for c in df.columns]\ndf["predicted_production"] = np.expm1(joblib.load(a.model).predict(df)).round(1)\nprint(df.to_string(index=False))\n', 'project4_crop_production/src/make_synthetic_data.py': '"""Generate a small synthetic dataset with the same schema as the project\ndescription. ONLY for smoke-testing the pipeline when the real data is absent."""\nimport numpy as np, pandas as pd, sys\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(42)\nn = 6000\ncrops = {"Rice": 3.0, "Wheat": 2.6, "Maize": 2.9, "Sesame": 0.4, "Cotton": 1.1, "Sugarcane": 70}\nstates = ["Andhra Pradesh", "Punjab", "Maharashtra", "Bihar", "Tamil Nadu", "Karnataka"]\nseasons = ["Kharif", "Rabi", "Whole Year", "Summer"]\ncrop = rng.choice(list(crops), n)\nstate = rng.choice(states, n)\nseason = rng.choice(seasons, n)\nyear = rng.integers(2001, 2015, n)\narea = rng.lognormal(7, 1.0, n)\nyield_ = np.array([crops[c] for c in crop]) * rng.normal(1, 0.15, n) * (1 + 0.02 * (year - 2001))\nprod = area * yield_\nprod[rng.random(n) < 0.03] = np.nan\npd.DataFrame({"State_Name": state, "Crop_Year": year, "Season": season,\n              "Crop": crop, "Area": area.round(1), "Production": prod.round(1)}\n             ).to_csv(sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "data/synthetic_crop_production.csv", index=False)\nprint("written")\n', 'project4_crop_production/src/train.py': '"""Project 4 - Prediction of Agriculture Crop Production in India (2001-2014).\n\nUsage:\n    python src/train.py --data data/crop_production.csv\nColumn names are auto-detected (case-insensitive) so it works with the\ndata.gov.in style file (State_Name, District_Name, Crop_Year, Season, Crop,\nArea, Production) as well as the column names in the project brief\n(Crop, Variety, State, Quantity, Season, Unit, Cost, Recommended Zone).\n"""\nimport argparse, json, re\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport joblib\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use("Agg")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import GradientBoostingRegressor, RandomForestRegressor\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\nfrom sklearn.metrics import mean_absolute_error, mean_squared_error, r2_score\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import GridSearchCV, train_test_split\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder, StandardScaler\n\n\ndef norm(c):\n    return re.sub(r"[^a-z0-9]+", "_", c.strip().lower()).strip("_")\n\n\ndef load(path):\n    df = pd.read_csv(path)\n    df.columns = [norm(c) for c in df.columns]\n    return df\n\n\ndef pick(df, *cands):\n    for c in cands:\n        if c in df.columns:\n            return c\n    return None\n\n\ndef prepare(df):\n    target = pick(df, "production", "production_tons", "production_in_tons")\n    if target is None:\n        raise SystemExit(f"No production column found. Columns: {list(df.columns)}")\n    df = df.copy()\n    df[target] = pd.to_numeric(df[target], errors="coerce")\n    df = df.dropna(subset=[target])\n    df = df[df[target] >= 0]\n\n    num = [c for c in [pick(df, "area", "quantity", "area_hectares"),\n                       pick(df, "crop_year", "year"),\n                       pick(df, "cost")] if c]\n    cat = [c for c in [pick(df, "state_name", "state"), pick(df, "district_name", "district"),\n                       pick(df, "season"), pick(df, "crop"), pick(df, "variety"),\n                       pick(df, "recommended_zone")] if c]\n    for c in num:\n        df[c] = pd.to_numeric(df[c], errors="coerce")\n    for c in cat:\n        df[c] = df[c].astype(str).str.strip()\n    # Heavy right-skew in production -> model log1p(production)\n    y = np.log1p(df[target])\n    return df[num + cat], y, df[target], num, cat, target\n\n\ndef build(model, num, cat):\n    pre = ColumnTransformer([\n        ("num", Pipeline([("imp", __import__("sklearn.impute", fromlist=["SimpleImputer"]).SimpleImputer(strategy="median")),\n                          ("sc", StandardScaler())]), num),\n        ("cat", OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown="ignore", min_frequency=5), cat),\n    ])\n    return Pipeline([("pre", pre), ("model", model)])\n\n\ndef evaluate(pipe, X, y_log, y_true, cap=None):\n    raw = pipe.predict(X)\n    if cap is not None:  # guard against linear-model extrapolation blowing up expm1\n        raw = np.clip(raw, 0, cap)\n    p = np.expm1(raw)\n    return {"R2_log": r2_score(y_log, np.log1p(p.clip(0))),\n            "R2": r2_score(y_true, p),\n            "RMSE": float(np.sqrt(mean_squared_error(y_true, p))),\n            "MAE": float(mean_absolute_error(y_true, p))}, p\n\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument("--data", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument("--out", default="outputs")\n    ap.add_argument("--seed", type=int, default=42)\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n    out = Path(a.out); out.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\n    df = load(a.data)\n    print(f"Loaded {df.shape[0]} rows, columns: {list(df.columns)}")\n    X, y_log, y_raw, num, cat, target = prepare(df)\n    print(f"Target={target} | numeric={num} | categorical={cat}")\n    Xtr, Xte, ytr, yte, rtr, rte = train_test_split(X, y_log, y_raw, test_size=0.2, random_state=a.seed)\n\n    models = {\n        "Ridge": (Ridge(alpha=1.0), {}),\n        "RandomForest": (RandomForestRegressor(random_state=a.seed, n_jobs=-1),\n                         {"model__n_estimators": [100, 200], "model__max_depth": [None, 20]}),\n        "GradientBoosting": (GradientBoostingRegressor(random_state=a.seed),\n                             {"model__n_estimators": [150, 300], "model__learning_rate": [0.05, 0.1],\n                              "model__max_depth": [3, 5]}),\n    }\n    results, best_name, best_pipe, best_r2 = {}, None, None, -np.inf\n    for name, (m, grid) in models.items():\n        pipe = build(m, num, cat)\n        if grid:\n            pipe = GridSearchCV(pipe, grid, cv=3, scoring="r2", n_jobs=-1).fit(Xtr, ytr).best_estimator_\n        else:\n            pipe.fit(Xtr, ytr)\n        metrics, pred = evaluate(pipe, Xte, yte, rte, cap=ytr.max() + 1)\n        results[name] = metrics\n        print(name, {k: round(v, 3) for k, v in metrics.items()})\n        if metrics["R2_log"] > best_r2:\n            best_name, best_pipe, best_r2, best_pred = name, pipe, metrics["R2_log"], pred\n\n    (out / "metrics.json").write_text(json.dumps({"best": best_name, "results": results}, indent=2))\n    joblib.dump(best_pipe, out / "best_model.joblib")\n\n    # Plots\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5, 5))\n    ax.scatter(np.log1p(rte), np.log1p(best_pred.clip(0)), s=4, alpha=.4)\n    lim = [0, max(np.log1p(rte).max(), np.log1p(best_pred.clip(0)).max())]\n    ax.plot(lim, lim, "r--"); ax.set(xlabel="Actual log(1+production)", ylabel="Predicted",\n                                      title=f"{best_name}: actual vs predicted")\n    fig.tight_layout(); fig.savefig(out / "actual_vs_predicted.png", dpi=150); plt.close(fig)\n\n    names = best_pipe.named_steps["pre"].get_feature_names_out()\n    mdl = best_pipe.named_steps["model"]\n    imp = getattr(mdl, "feature_importances_", None)\n    if imp is None:\n        imp = np.abs(mdl.coef_)\n    top = pd.Series(imp, index=names).sort_values().tail(15)\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 5)); top.plot.barh(ax=ax)\n    ax.set_title("Top 15 features"); fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(out / "feature_importance.png", dpi=150); plt.close(fig)\n\n    # Model comparison\n    cmp = pd.DataFrame(results).T\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 4)); cmp["R2_log"].plot.bar(ax=ax)\n    ax.set_ylabel("R2 (log scale)"); ax.set_title("Model comparison"); fig.tight_layout()\n    fig.savefig(out / "model_comparison.png", dpi=150); plt.close(fig)\n    print(f"Best model: {best_name}. Outputs in {out}/")\n\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n'}
